  mapId: MAP-051
  displayName: The Divide
  environment: Mountain Pass
  warfareFocus: Strategic chokepoint warfare
  executiveSummary: High-altitude mountain-pass battlefield for strategic chokepoint warfare, elevation-driven combat, autonomous route control, and multi-domain coordination across narrow high-risk terrain.
  designGoals:
  - name: Chokepoint-Focused Warfare
    description: 
  - name: 
    description: Mountain passes and switchbacks determine movement and convoy access.
  - name: 
    description: 
  - name: 
    description: High ground creates decisive overwatch, artillery, and sensor advantages.
  - name: 
    description: 
  - name: 
    description: Narrow exposed routes enable ambushes and deliberate route denial.
  - name: 
    description: 
  - name: 
    description: Units account for elevation, cliffs, rock hazards, fog, and route exposure.
  - name: 
    description: 
  - name: 
    description: Mountain fog and rock occlusion degrade sensors and communications.
  - name: 
    description: 
  - name: 
    description: Severe terrain constraints make route selection, convoy protection, and relay control critical.
  deployment: Fixed deployment budget ~10,000 points. Blue deploys from southwest lower-pass gate; Red deploys from northeast ridge-top fortress.
